# Example redirects.map — generated by: wp pgds build-redirects --out=/etc/nginx/redirects.map
#
# Format: <old_path>  <target_url>;
# One rule per line, terminated with a semicolon. Included from a map{} block in
# pgds.conf, so it must contain map entries only — no server/location directives.
#
# After regenerating:  nginx -t && systemctl reload nginx
#
# IMPORTANT: /etc/nginx/redirects.map must EXIST before pgds.conf is loaded, even if
# empty. `include` is a hard dependency and nginx refuses to start without it:
#   [emerg] open() "/etc/nginx/redirects.map" failed (2: No such file or directory)
# user_data.sh touches an empty one on first boot for exactly this reason, because the
# real map is only generated after the 2,000-post import (§9.4).
#
# Why a map instead of a redirect plugin (§9.4): 2,000 rules in the database would be
# consulted on every request. Nginx resolves a map in constant time, before PHP starts.

/tin-tuc/dai-le-phat-dan-2570.html          /dai-le-phat-dan-pl-2570/;
/chuyen-muc/song-an-lanh/an-chay-dung.html  /an-chay-dung-cach/;
/p/12345                                    /kien-truc-chua-co-bac-bo/;
